0</year>. Insolubility of lipids in triton X-100: physical origin and relationship to sphingolipid/cholesterol membrane domains (rafts). <source>Biochim. Biophys. Acta.</source> <volume>1508</volume>:<fpage>182</fpage>&#x02013;195.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11090825</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal">Vonakis, B.M., H. Chen, H. Haleem-Smith, and H. Metzger. <year>1997</year>. The unique domain as the site on Lyn kinase for its constitutive association with the high affinity receptor for IgE. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>272</volume>:<fpage>24072</fpage>&#x02013;24080.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9295361</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal">Xu, X., R. Bittman, G. Duportail, D. Heissler, C. Vilcheze, and E. London. <year>2001</year>. Effect of the structure of natural sterols and sphingolipids on the formation of ordered sphingolipid/sterol domains (rafts). Comparison of cholesterol to plant, fungal, and disease-associated sterols and comparison of sphingomyelin, cerebrosides, and ceramide. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>276</volume>:<fpage>33540</fpage>&#x02013;33546.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11432870</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal">Ramstedt, B., and J.P. Slotte. <year>1999</year>. Comparison of the biophysical properties of racemic and d-erythro-N-acyl sphingomyelins. <source>Biophys. J.</source> <volume>77</volume>:<fpage>1498</fpage>&#x02013;1506.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10465760</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal">Horejsi, V. <year>2002</year>. Membrane rafts in immunoreceptor signaling: new doubts, new proofs? <source>Trends Immunol.</source> <volume>23</volume>:<fpage>562</fpage>&#x02013;564.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12464560</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal">Field, K.A., D. Holowka, and B. Baird. <year>1995</year>. Fc&#x0025b;RI-mediated recruitment of p53/56lyn to detergent-resistant membrane domains accompanies cellular signaling. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>92</volume>:<fpage>9201</fpage>&#x02013;9205.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7568101</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal">Kovarova, M., P. Tolar, R. Arudchandran, L. Draberova, J. Rivera, and P. Draber. <year>2001</year>. Structure-function analysis of Lyn kinase association with lipid rafts and initiation of early signaling events after Fc&#x0025b; receptor I aggregation. <source>Mol. Cell. Biol.</source> <volume>21</volume>:<fpage>8318</fpage>&#x02013;8328.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11713268</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal">Law, C.L., K.A. Chandran, S.P. Sidorenko, and E.A. Clark. <year>1996</year>. Phospholipase C-&#x003b3;1 interacts with conserved phosphotyrosyl residues in the linker region of Syk and is a substrate for Syk. <source>Mol. Cell. Biol.</source> <volume>16</volume>:<fpage>1305</fpage>&#x02013;1315.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8657103</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal">Keshvara, L.M., C.C. Isaacson, T.M. Yankee, R. Sarac, M.L. Harrison, and R.L. Geahlen. <year>1998</year>. Syk- and Lyn-dependent phosphorylation of Syk on multiple tyrosines following B cell activation includes a site that negatively regulates signaling. <source>J. Immunol.</source> <volume>161</volume>:<fpage>5276</fpage>&#x02013;5283.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9820500</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal">Rivera, J. <year>2002</year>. Molecular adapters in Fc&#x0025b;RI signaling and the allergic response. <source>Curr. Opin. Immunol.</source> <volume>14</volume>:<fpage>688</fpage>&#x02013;693.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12413516</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal">Saitoh, S., S. Odom, G. Gomez, C.L. Sommers, H.A. Young, J. Rivera, and L.E. Samelson. <year>2003</year>. The four distal tyrosines are required for LAT-dependent signaling in Fc&#x0025b;RI-mediated mast cell activation. <source>J. Exp. Med.</source> <volume>198</volume>:<fpage>831</fpage>&#x02013;843.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12953098</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal">Odom, S., G. Gomez, M. Kovarova, Y. Furumoto, J.J. Ryan, H.V. Wright, C. Gonzalez-Espinosa, M.L. Hibbs, K.W. Harder, and J. Rivera. <year>2004</year>. Negative regulation of immunoglobulin E&#x02013;dependent allergic responses by Lyn kinase. <source>J. Exp. Med.</source> <volume>199</volume>:<fpage>1491</fpage>&#x02013;1502.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15173205</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal">Hernandez-Hansen, V., A.J. Smith, Z. Surviladze, A. Chigaev, T. Mazel, J. Kalesnikoff, C.A. Lowell, G. Krystal, L.A. Sklar, B.S. Wilson, and J.M. Oliver. <year>2004</year>. Dysregulated Fc&#x0025b;RI signaling and altered Fyn and SHIP activities in Lyn-deficient mast cells. <source>J. Immunol.</source> <volume>173</volume>:<fpage>100</fpage>&#x02013;112.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15210764</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal">Parravicini, V., M. Gadina, M. Kovarova, S. Odom, C. Gonzalez-Espinosa, Y. Furumoto, S. Saitoh, L.E. Samelson, J.J. O'Shea, and J. Rivera. <year>2002</year>. Fyn kinase initiates complementary signals required for IgE-dependent mast cell degranulation. <source>Nat. Immunol.</source> <volume>3</volume>:<fpage>741</fpage>&#x02013;748.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12089510</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal">Gu, H., K. Saito, L.D. Klaman, J. Shen, T. Fleming, Y. Wang, J.C. Pratt, G. Lin, B. Lim,